  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>P2T07 - EN override vs overload</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><em>(English)</em> What is the difference between <strong>overriding</strong> and <strong>overloading</strong>?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Overriding redefines a parent method (same signature) in a subclass; overloading is same name, different parameters in the same class.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>0.2500000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Overriding redefines a parent method; overloading is same name with different parameters]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[Correct.]]></text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[They are two names for the same thing]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[They are different concepts.]]></text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[Overloading needs inheritance; overriding does not]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[It is the opposite: overriding needs inheritance.]]></text></feedback></answer>
  </question>

